## Fixed wire syntax, independent of the methods and types in a schema.
## Calls and value calls keep their words and slots neutral: the checker
## decides which method, named type, or `INTRINSIC FUNCTION`, such as
## `Duration`'s `1 hours 30 minutes`, they mean. A variant is
## marked with a backtick, `` `red ``, so a value call is never one.
ENTRY [ONE OR MORE: call],

call: ANYFIX CALL [ARGUMENTS: ZERO OR MORE: argument],
argument: ONE OF [
  annotated: ANYFIX CALL [value, WORD "AS", type],
  value,
],
value: ONE OF [
  integer: NUMBER [WRITTEN INTEGER],
  float: NUMBER [WRITTEN FLOAT],
  text: STRING,
  list: SQUARE BRACKET [ZERO OR MORE: value],
  braces: CURLY BRACE [ZERO OR MORE: entry],
  variant: variant,
  call: value call,
],
## A variant, written with a backtick before its shape: `` `red ``,
## `` `missing (File Id "a") ``, `` `(1 + 1) ``. The backtick is a symbol
## word, so in an argument the variant is parenthesized: `` paint (`red) ``.
variant: ANYFIX CALL [WORD "`", body: value call],
## A call that isn't marked as a variant: a named type's constructor,
## `File Id "a"`, a record's field, or a function.
value call: ANYFIX CALL [NAME [NO KEYWORD, MATCHING REGEX "^[^`]"], ARGUMENTS: ZERO OR MORE: value],
## In braces, a map's entry is a key and a value. A record's entry is a
## value, and the checker reads from the record's fields which one it
## fills: `path "a"` is the call `path _`,
## `changed more than (1 hours) ago` a field's shape, and a variant,
## `` `by name ``, the value of the field without a name whose type has it.
entry: ONE OF [
  map: ANYFIX CALL [key: STRING, value],
  value,
],

## These rules are the schema language's type rules, including generic
## types, but for `UNION`: an annotation names a type its value is written
## in, and a union's member is told by its form alone. A test keeps them in
## step with protocol.grammar.anyx.
type: ONE OF [
  refined: refined type,
  list: list type,
  map: map type,
  named: reference,
],
refined type: ANYFIX CALL [base: type, WORD "WHERE", predicate: SQUARE BRACKET [ONE OR MORE: term]],

## A predicate's term: the value it tests, `_`, a parameter's name, a
## constant, or a function of terms. Which function a call means, such as
## `_ <= _ < _` or `_ ends with _`, the checker reads from the prelude's
## `FUNCTION`s: `[10 <= _ < 30]`, `` [_ and (`true)] ``,
## `` [items . has at most one of [`any case, `_ encoding]] ``.
term: ONE OF [
  subject: UNDERSCORE,
  integer: NUMBER [WRITTEN INTEGER],
  float: NUMBER [WRITTEN FLOAT],
  text: STRING,
  variants: SQUARE BRACKET [ZERO OR MORE: term variant],
  variant: term variant,
  call: ANYFIX CALL [NAME [NO KEYWORD, MATCHING REGEX "^[^`]"], ARGUMENTS: ZERO OR MORE: term],
],
## A variant in a predicate, `` `true ``, or a variant's shape with `_` in
## each slot, `` `_ encoding ``.
term variant: ANYFIX CALL [WORD "`", body: ANYFIX CALL [NAME [NO KEYWORD], ARGUMENTS: ZERO OR MORE: UNDERSCORE]],
list type: ANYFIX CALL [WORD "LIST", item: type],
map type: ANYFIX CALL [WORD "MAP", value: type],
reference: ANYFIX CALL [NAME [NO KEYWORD], ARGUMENTS: ZERO OR MORE: type],
